      "message": "Thanks for the updates in PS 2! `SkLRUCache` with 4096 entries and removing `OneLineShaper::fFallbackFonts` looks great.\n\nOne small addition for thread safety: we are currently landing https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1400636 (`[skparagraph] Make FontCollection thread-safe`), which guards `FaceCache` and `VariationCache` with an internal `SkMutex` inside each pimpl struct (since engine embedders like Flutter\u0027s `ImpellerTypographyContext` share a single `FontCollection` across worker threads).\n\nBecause `SkLRUCache::find()` relinks the entry to the front of its doubly-linked list even on a cache hit, could you add an `SkMutex fMutex;` inside `FontCollection::FallbackCache` with small `find` / `insert` / `reset` helpers (similar to `ParagraphCache`)? That way we keep the `SkLRUCache` eviction behavior and make `FallbackCache` thread-safe out of the box.",
